A busy morning brings reports with similar words but sometimes different causes. Keep one
ticket per established cause, with an auditable count of distinct report IDs.

## The rule

A report belongs with another when evidence supports the **same cause**
([decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause), which supersedes the unchanged historical decision 0001):

1. Keep one copy of each report ID; preserve the body, tenant, channel and timestamps.
2. Resolve the tenant's locale and booking-form version. For day-first tenants, booking-v3 form reports route to the hint issue; other supported paths route to the parser issue.
3. Compare causes, not subjects or browser-based intake tags. Unknown tenant, unsupported locale, conflicting evidence or unexplained symptoms require investigation, not an automatic merge.
4. Keep one issue per established cause, update its distinct-ID count, and verify each fix separately. See the [#4471 split](/kb/incidents/4471-split) for issue links and unresolved reports.

**Closure check:** the course now reports #4471 closed on 5 October: parser **fixed**,
hint **won't fix — booking-v3 form retired**. Do not call retirement a repair. Before attaching
a new report to either closed issue, check the current form/version and reproduce it. A
post-fix report or use of a retired form needs investigation and a linked follow-up or reopening,
not automatic merging into history.

<Callout>
Do not keep applying the old subject-only rule while the desk works. Matching words do not establish matching causes.
</Callout>

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## When you are unsure

Keep the report visible and unmerged until the cause is supported. An intake tag is a guess,
and a calculated cause does not explain every unusual symptom. Investigate before closure.
